a California businessman is opening his  heart and wallet to high school students  and teachers after the fire disaster in  the town of Paradise he gave students  and staff at Paradise High School $1,000  each  well altogether the donations told it  totaled more than 1 million dollars and  as Jamie yuccas shows us the men  contributing the money says his only  connection to the school is emotional  smiles have been hard to come by for  these paradise high school students  ever since suffering through the most  devastating wildfire in California  history 90 year old real estate  developer Bob Wilson lives near San  Diego but when he heard about the  hardships these students were enduring  he felt compelled to help about 900 of  the 980 young people attending Paradise  High School lost their homes for me high  school was idyllic time of my life you  might say so I thought about these kids  and I thought about my experience and I  said you know if I can just put a smile  on their face and so I decided on the  spot I would do this  Wilson felt the best way he could have a  personal positive impact was through  individual donations he's giving a  thousand dollar check to all 980  students and their 105 teachers and  staff members and then the more I  thought about it and I thought what  about the whole school what about the  teachers what about the bus driver the  janitor and so forth and so I said I  would include the entire school a lot of  kids will just turn the checks over to  their families for just basic essential  items like food and gas Wilson says  handing out more than a million dollars  is making him feel like a million bucks  let's face it you know there's joy in  giving and especially when you do it  directly he doesn't even know us but he  has it as far  to give us money to us to just help us  and it kind of two hearts mile for CBS  this morning  Jamie yuccas Los Angeles a lot of  smiling hearts in Paradise nice to hear  of a big heart as well when you've lost  everything you know and you have someone  who says here you go here you go no  strings attached just do something for  yourself again shout out to Bob Wilson
 

